// The signature says what the function returns and the brackets say
// what the body hands back, so the two disagreeing is settled before
// anything runs.  Reporting it at the definition means it is reported
// whether or not the function is ever called — nothing here calls it.
fn returns_a_scalar() → u32:
    [1, 2, 3]

@start
fn main() → ∅:
    std.println("not reached")
